To generate an automatic table of contents (TOC) in a LaTeX document, you need to follow these steps:

1. Add the `toc` option in the document class declaration:

   ```
   \documentclass[toc]{article}
   ```

   or

   ```
   \documentclass[toc]{book}
   ```

2. Add the `\tableofcontents` command in the document preamble, just after the `\begin{document}` command:

   ```
   \begin{document}
     \tableofcontents
     ...
   \end{document}
   ```

3. Add the `\section`, `\subsection`, or any other sectional unit command where you want to add a section, subsection, or any other sectional unit.

   ```
   \section{Introduction}
   ...

   \subsection{Background}
   ...

   \section{Methodology}
   ...

   \subsection{Data Collection}
   ...

   \section{Results}
   ...

   \subsection{Analysis}
   ...
   ```

4. Add the `hyperref` package to create hyperlinks in the TOC:

   ```
   \usepackage{hyperref}
   ```

5. Compile your LaTeX document twice to update the TOC.

